From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] spl: getf() starts at, and releasefp() sets, the descriptor's offset

The macOS layer's getf() starts every descriptor at offset 0 and never
moves it: XNU gives a kext no access to a descriptor's offset. zfs receive
reads the stream through the descriptor's vnode after libzfs has read
the BEGIN record from it, so zfs receive < file read the BEGIN record
again as the next record and failed with "invalid backup stream" (the
OpenZFS test suite's zfs_send and zfs_receive groups, P3-01 checkpoint 2);
zfs send -R > file wrote over libzfs's own header. NeoDarwin's kernel
exports file_offset_get() and file_offset_set() (kernel patch 0042):
getf() starts a regular file at the process's offset, and releasefp(),
from the same process, leaves it after what the module read or wrote, as
the FreeBSD and Linux layers' zfs_file_read() and zfs_file_write() do.
Pipes still go through libzfs's FIFO relay (libzfs_macos_wrapfd()).

Rebase-risk: low (getf and releasefp only)
---
diff --git a/module/os/neodarwin/spl/spl-vnode.c b/module/os/neodarwin/spl/spl-vnode.c
--- a/module/os/neodarwin/spl/spl-vnode.c
+++ b/module/os/neodarwin/spl/spl-vnode.c
@@ -168,6 +168,11 @@
     vfs_context_t ctx);
 extern int file_vnode_withvid(int, struct vnode **, uint32_t *);
 extern int file_drop(int);
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+/* NeoDarwin's BSD KPI (kernel patch 0042). */
+extern int file_offset_get(int, off_t *);
+extern int file_offset_set(int, off_t);
+#endif
 
 /*
  * getf(int fd) - hold a lock on a file descriptor, to be released by calling
@@ -216,6 +221,19 @@
 		if (type == VCHR || type == VBLK) {
 			sfp->f_file = minor(vnode_specrdev(vp));
 		}
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+		/*
+		 * Start where the process's own I/O left a regular file
+		 * (zfs receive < file: libzfs has read the BEGIN record);
+		 * releasefp() leaves the descriptor after what the module
+		 * read or wrote, as FreeBSD's and Linux's file I/O does.
+		 */
+		if (type == VREG) {
+			off_t off;
+			if (file_offset_get(fd, &off) == 0)
+				sfp->f_offset = off;
+		}
+#endif
 		file_drop(fd);
 	}
 
@@ -243,6 +261,11 @@
 void
 releasefp(struct spl_fileproc *fp)
 {
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+	if (fp->f_vnode != NULL && vnode_vtype(fp->f_vnode) == VREG &&
+	    fp->f_proc == current_proc())
+		(void) file_offset_set(fp->f_fd, fp->f_offset);
+#endif
 	if (fp->f_vnode != NULL)
 		vnode_put(fp->f_vnode);
 
